# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and never committed.
# Only one key is needed; the first one found wins.
GROQ_API_KEY=
# CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# Which model rewrites scene text into a music style, and where it lives.
# Unset means openai/gpt-oss-20b on Groq. The two go together: a Cerebras model
# name sent to Groq's URL is a 401, so set both when switching provider.
# LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# LLM_ENDPOINT=https://api.cerebras.ai/v1/chat/completions

# Reasoning effort, passed through as typed because providers disagree on the
# words: gpt-oss wants low/medium/high, qwen3 wants none/default. Unset means
# low. Use `off` to send no such field at all, which no provider can refuse.
# LLM_EFFORT=low

# start.sh reads the rest of this file too, so a session is just ./start.sh.
# Anything already set in the environment wins over what is here, which is what
# keeps a one-off MUSIC_TOKEN=... ./start.sh working.

# Shared secret between the server and Foundry. Set one whenever the port is
# reachable from the internet, which it is the moment a tunnel is up.
# MUSIC_TOKEN=

# A named Cloudflare tunnel, for an address that survives restarts. Both are
# needed: the token authenticates the tunnel, the hostname is what you routed to
# http://localhost:30001 in its config. Without them you get a quick tunnel on a
# random hostname that changes every run.
# CF_TUNNEL_TOKEN=
# MUSIC_HOSTNAME=
